What is sorting?:Sorting means arranging values according to an order
Ascending order: [7, 2, 9, 1, 5] -> [1, 2, 5, 7, 9]
Descending order: [9, 7, 5, 2, 1]

For example:
-> Binary search requires sorted data
-> Duplicate detection becomes easier
-> Minimum and maximum values become organized
-> Intervals can be merged efficiently
-> Results can be ranked
-> Records can be grouped by category, date, price, or priority

Types of sorting algorithms:
A. Comparison-based sorting: Comparison-based algorithms decide order by comparing two values
Typical comparisons are:a < b
                        a > b
                        a <= b
